# npm runs `node-gyp rebuild` for any dependency that ships a binding.gyp, even
# when the package sets `gypfile: false`. better-sqlite3 does exactly that, while
# also shipping working N-API prebuilds — so the compile is unnecessary, and it
# fails on any machine without a C++ toolchain (which includes the Windows CI
# runner).
#
# Scripts are therefore skipped by default, and the two binaries that genuinely
# need fetching are handled by `npm run setup`:
#   - Electron's binary, because electron@43 ships no postinstall of its own
#   - nothing else: esbuild and better-sqlite3 both ship platform prebuilds
ignore-scripts=true
